// The address of a function the program defines with `...` cannot be taken: a
// call through a pointer passes its arguments in fixed slots, and a variadic
// function takes its extra ones as a list, so the call would land on the wrong
// parameters. The callee of a direct call is not an address (chk_cal holds its node).
chk_vaval(string name, int id) {
  int i = find_str((import fnames), name);
  if(i >= 0 && fn_variadic(i) == 1 && frame_off(name) < 0 && (import chk_cal)[0] != id) {
    diag_node(id, "the address of '" + name + "', a function this program defines with '...', is taken: a call through a pointer cannot pass the extra arguments; wrap it in a function of its own");
  }
} return void;
